# On a Nix account, identity comes from git, which agenix populated from
# secrets/personal/git-config.age:
jj config set --user user.name  "$(git config --get user.name)"
jj config set --user user.email "$(git config --get user.email)"

# That does NOT work on the mise account. tools/git/config is shared with the
# Nix profiles and deliberately carries no [user] block, so both reads return
# an empty string and the identity is silently set to "". There, gh is the
# only source:
#
#   mise run identity
#
# which also fills in ~/.gitconfig, since git has the same gap and only
# notices it at commit time rather than at `jj git init`.

# Where these land, and the trap. `jj config set --user` writes
# ~/.config/jj/config.toml, but jj merges ~/.config/jj/conf.d/*.toml OVER
# that file. A [user] block in conf.d therefore beats every later
# `jj config set --user` with no warning. Verified on jj 0.45.1.
jj config path --user    # prints both the file and the conf.d directory
jj config list user      # what actually won
